format session-log-v1
stamp 20260819.182041
editor Claude Code
model claude-opus-5
voice Kyri
host Vultr SEA NixOS VPS ai-jail pier (Daylight DC-1 hand) -- Eastern (EDT)
title Caravan rolling -- rolling never creates room, it names who was holding it
prompt Kyri voice and Radiant first, then REMEMBER, the itineraries, and the newest log recommends; close open agent-closable reds Standfast-first, then take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; send each finished increment as its own signed round
think Standfast first. REDS living rows are 80, 83, 84, 85. Rows 83, 84, 85 read closed with witnesses on metal, and 85's wider sweep closed for real on 20260819.134229. Row 80's booked loom -- a witness asserting the crypto file count and the suite registration count are one computed number -- turned out to already stand as tools/crypto_count_guard_witness.rish, so I ran it rather than trusting the ledger prose. GREEN on metal: 80 crypto/*.rye files, each registered in the suite and each registration naming a real file, a bijection rather than a bare tally. No agent-closable red stood open, so the constructive queue opened.
think The crux was named by the last lap's recommend and by REMEMBER's live edge: whether a supervisor may run the widest set AND refill a slot as each child finishes, rather than reaping a whole stage before the next begins -- the rolling cohort, where the safe-reaping rule and the room have to hold at once.
think The first move was to see that the safe rule was never what it looked like. cohort.rye reaped every stage whole, and the reason it gave was that one early verdict strands a pair. Read again, the rule is narrower than the discipline that enforced it: it forbids a verdict leaving while a sibling runs, and says nothing at all about when a child may be waited on. So reaping and reporting are two acts, and rolling keeps the rule exactly by splitting them -- reap eagerly to free a slot, hold every verdict until the queue drains.
think The second move was admission. A queue is ordered, and in these documents order is meaning: an ask is placed before it is passed and passed before it comes home. So a rolling supervisor may not reach past a blocked head for a later item that happens to fit -- head-of-line only. That single restraint is what makes the finding sharp, because it means the order can hold the room shut no matter how eager the supervisor is.
think The third move was to count the waste by its cause rather than in one lump. A slot standing empty with work queued is idle BY BARRIER when the discipline alone forbade the fill, and idle BY ORDER when the head conflicts with a domain still running. That split is the whole measurement, and it is deterministic -- no wall-clock, no scheduling race, so the witness proves a property rather than a stopwatch.
think I predicted both runs on paper before building, and the paper said something I did not expect: over the flattened nine-assignment lap the two disciplines wait the SAME two turns. Staged calls them barriers; rolling calls them the order. The slot stands empty either way, because every stage boundary in serial_three_clients.bron is also a conflict boundary -- the virtualiser touches all three clients and may never stand beside itself. So rolling converts no waiting into work there. What it does is prove who was doing the waiting.
think That made the second queue necessary rather than decorative: a queue whose order agrees with the isolation the document already has. Three clients placing twice each into the regions they own touch nothing of one another, so the head is admissible at every turn and a freed slot fills at once -- two idle turns staged become zero rolling, same document, same bound of three. A client's second item still waits for its own first, which is the head-of-line rule doing its plainest work: a domain never runs beside itself.
think Both disciplines were built as one program differing in one line -- rolling may fill whenever a slot is free, staged may fill only an empty table -- so a difference in the report is a difference in the discipline rather than in two programs that happen to disagree. Both reap one child per turn.
think The first build of the refill queue reached for the peek verb to give each client a second, read-only item. It came back malformed, and the reason was honest rather than a bug: gap.attempt answers place, pass, and home, and refuses the other three verbs outright rather than half-carrying them under a fall reading. Swapped to a second place per client, which is truer to the point anyway -- the same verb, twice, so nothing about the comparison rests on a verb's peculiarity.
obs The sharpest result is the one I did not go looking for: rolling never creates room. It removes the supervisor as a cause of waiting and leaves the document's own order standing exactly where it was. On the ordered lap the total idle turns are equal, 2 and 2; only the attribution moves. A cheaper supervisor would have reported a win there and been wrong.
obs The honest limit of hosted ground is named in the module rather than hidden: a supervisor waits on a child it can name, so it reaps the eldest, and a long-running eldest holds a slot its younger siblings have already freed. A true wait-on-any would tighten this; the ground does not offer one yet, and pretending otherwise would make the numbers a claim rather than a measurement.
obs Reuse over restatement: cohort.rye's spawn_one, reap_one, Running, and run_child were opened pub rather than copied, so the child contract and the spawn path are one implementation across both rungs. The pair predicate came from concurrent.rye whole, one more size up, unchanged for the third rung running.
obs The TAME long-function ratchet named run_queue at 116 lines on the first pass. Split at its natural seams -- a Table holding the turn's state, fill_table for the head-of-line admission, reap_oldest for the wait and the close, drain_late for the hygiene the loose reading alone needs -- and the ratchet no longer names it. A compound assert was caught by the bans and split so the failing half names itself.
loom witness=caravan_rolling ordered_idle_staged=2 ordered_idle_rolling=2 ordered_barrier_staged=2 ordered_order_rolling=2 refill_idle_staged=2 refill_idle_rolling=0 peak_in_flight=3 children=6 asks_home=6 stranded_loose=2 stranded_held=0
file caravan/rolling.rye the rung -- two disciplines one line apart, head-of-line admission, verdicts held to the drain, waste counted by its cause
file tools/caravan_rolling_witness.rish the proof on metal -- every check native contains, order-independent, no shell grep over interpolated output
file caravan/cohort.rye spawn_one, reap_one, Running, and run_child opened pub so the child contract is one implementation across both rungs
file caravan/README.md the ladder table gains its rung and the prose gains the finding, in the same commit as the code
file crux/REMEMBER.md the live edge moves to rolling and the cohort edge folds into the prior-edges paragraph, so the card stays single-stranded
recommend keep-going the wait-on-any question -- whether a supervisor that could be told which child finished, rather than choosing which to wait on, would convert any of the order-idle turns the eldest-first reaping leaves standing, or whether the order holds them shut regardless
